            "<strong>Gloves and PPE</strong>: use them for the indications and not beyond (gloves are not needed for a pulse or an oral drug); forecast consumption from the stock card and requisition before the reorder level; keep an emergency reserve for deliveries, spills and isolation; never wash and reuse single-use gloves; report stock-outs as incidents so that they are counted.",
            "<strong>Sterilisation</strong>: one working autoclave with a log beats three broken ones; prioritise critical items; high-level disinfection by boiling for semi-critical items where no autoclave exists; condemn torn and damp packs even when the shelf is bare.",
            "<strong>Staffing and occupancy</strong>: two patients to a bed and floor beds are IPC failures (core component 7) — document them, cohort by organism where unavoidable, and present the bed-occupancy and infection figures together to management.",
            "<strong>Improvise safely, never unsafely</strong>: a chlorine solution made from locally bought bleach by the dilution formula, a sharps container from a rigid plastic bottle on a home visit, a cross-ventilated side room instead of a negative-pressure suite — all acceptable; a boiled catheter, a reused needle, a shared nebuliser mask or an unlabelled disinfectant bowl — never.",
